 The orchestrator wires your executor via the `ExecutorAdapter` interface
 (`runtime/abi/src/types.ts`). On day 1 (single-container) the orchestrator
 `SubProcessAdapter` spawns `node <executor-dist>/index.js` as a child
 process. For multi-container deployments, swap in a `DockerRunAdapter` or
 `K8sJobAdapter` — the ABI contract is identical either way.
+---
+
+## Changelog
+
+### ABI version 0.3 (executor-self-briefing feature)
+
+**Breaking change**: `briefingPath` / `BRIEFING_PATH` removed from `ExecutorInput`.
+
+Executors must now read their task specification directly from the management repo
+clone at `${EXECUTOR_WORKDIR}/mgmt` (self-briefing). The orchestrator no longer
+writes a briefing file or passes `BRIEFING_PATH` as an env var.
+
+Migration: replace `BRIEFING_PATH` reads with reads from
+`${EXECUTOR_WORKDIR}/mgmt/docs/features/<featureId>/tasks/<taskId>.yaml` and
+`${EXECUTOR_WORKDIR}/mgmt/docs/features/<featureId>/tasks.md`.
+
+The `BriefingTransportPort` interface has also been removed from the ABI package.
